Title: The Kerlaouen Light
Credit: Written by
Author: Inès Morvan
Draft date: October 7, 2026

INT. LIGHTHOUSE, LANTERN ROOM - NIGHT [[cosmos:k3x9a7bq2m]]

The lamp is cold. On the console, a leather-bound logbook lies open.

INÈS
(under her breath)
That’s dated yesterday.

She turns the page. The handwriting stops mid-sentence.

HUGO (O.S.)
Inès? Are you up there?

INÈS (CONT'D)
Don’t come up.

CUT TO:

EXT. ISLET - DAWN

The tide uncovers the causeway. Hugo waits, an unlit lantern in his hand.

HUGO (V.O.)
I should have gone up.
